<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Sitting Bull returns five weeks after his preventive visit, with the interpreter. His pain on walking has crept up to 4 of 10 as the injection wears off, eleven weeks after it was given; he still walks and rides with the brace. He has eaten less flour, lard and sugar and more bison and vegetables from the food distribution program and his garden, and he has joined the walking group run by the diabetes prevention program as far as his foot allows. His stool test and the HIV and hepatitis C tests were negative; the hepatitis B test showed he is not immune. He says his own ways of healing are part of how he is doing; he did not describe them, and the clinic did not ask. He would like his Tdap and hepatitis B vaccines today. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Pain</td><td>4 of 10 on walking</td></tr><tr><td>Function</td><td>Foot and Ankle Ability Measure, daily activities, 76%</td></tr><tr><td>Hemoglobin A1c</td><td>5.8%, from 6.0%</td></tr><tr><td>Screening results</td><td>Stool test, HIV and hepatitis C negative; not immune to hepatitis B</td></tr><tr><td>Food</td><td>Food distribution program and a larger garden</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

