    <title>Problems</title>
    <text><table><thead><tr><th>Problem</th><th>Clinical status</th><th>Verification</th><th>Code</th><th>Provenance</th></tr></thead><tbody>
  <tr ID="problem-1">
    <td>Chronic pain of the left ankle and hindfoot with a limp, for many years since an old gunshot wound to the foot, worse over the past two years: pain 7 of 10 on walking, stiffness in the mornings, walking limited to about half a mile; cause to be confirmed by imaging</td><td>resolved</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>M25.572</td><td>S — Synthetic presenting problem anchored to his documented foot wound and lifelong limp; resolved into the diagnosis at the consultation. Not a claim about his real symptoms.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-2">
    <td>Post-traumatic osteoarthritis of the left posterior subtalar and talonavicular joints after an old gunshot wound to the foot, confirmed by weight-bearing X-rays and CT; managed without surgery by his choice</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>M19.172</td><td>S — Synthetic modern diagnosis made at the consultation. Not a claim about his real joints.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-3">
    <td>Small retained metal fragments in the soft tissue of the left heel, outside the joints, from the old gunshot wound; blood lead normal (2.4 ug/dL); left in place</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>Z18.12</td><td>S — Synthetic CT finding anchored to the documented gunshot wound to the foot.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-4">
    <td>Raised blood pressure reading at intake (136/86 mmHg) without a diagnosis of hypertension; home readings planned</td><td>resolved</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>R03.0</td><td>S — Synthetic screening finding; resolved at the consultation visit when home readings averaged 124/78 mmHg.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-5">
    <td>Prediabetes (hemoglobin A1c 6.0%), found on diabetes screening</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>R73.03</td><td>S — Synthetic screening result in a man whose diet changed from buffalo and hunting to rations and farming; not a claim about his real health.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-6">
    <td>Food insecurity: food runs short at the end of each month; the household relies on commodity foods and what the family grows</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>Z59.41</td><td>S — Synthetic social need anchored to the documented loss of the buffalo and reservation farming.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-7">
    <td>Epigastric burning (dyspepsia) after six weeks of naproxen, without alarm features; hemoglobin unchanged; H. pylori stool antigen negative; resolved after stopping naproxen and four weeks of omeprazole</td><td>resolved</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>R10.13</td><td>S — Synthetic adverse effect of an NSAID; not a historical claim.</td>
  </tr></tbody></table></text>

